<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sungai Ujong</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sungai Ujong was a Minangkabau chiefdom on the west coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, one of the states of the Negeri Sembilan confederacy, centred on modern Seremban. Rivalries over its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> mines brought British intervention in 1874, and it became part of the reconstituted Negeri Sembilan under British protection in 1895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sungai-ujong.jpg" alt="Sungai Ujong" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shaqil Zikri · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seremban_skyline_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
